# LiteBus conventions

Follow these rules when editing shipping code under `src/`. See `AGENTS.md` for XML documentation requirements.

## Background services

| Concern | Where it lives |
| :--- | :--- |
| Contract | `IBackgroundService` (`ExecuteAsync`) in `LiteBus.Runtime.Abstractions` |
| Host manifest | `IModuleConfiguration.RegisterBackgroundService` |
| Generic host bridge | `BackgroundServiceHostAdapter` in `*.Hosting` extension packages |
| Feature loops | `*BackgroundService`, `AmqpInboxConsumer`, `*SchemaInitializer` |

Builder APIs: `EnableInboxProcessor`, `EnableOutboxProcessor`, `DisableSchemaInitialization`, `DisableIngressConsumer`. Do not use Runnable naming in code or docs.

## Modules and packages

- One primary module per feature area; optional builder for configuration.
- Transport-neutral core (`LiteBus.Inbox`, `LiteBus.Outbox`) must not reference hosting packages.
- Extension method classes: `ModuleRegistryExtensions` in the feature assembly namespace.
- Project names: `LiteBus.{Feature}` or `LiteBus.{Feature}.{Capability}` (for example `LiteBus.Inbox.Ingress.Amqp`).

## Interfaces and semantics

- Prefer small interfaces with clear nouns; one obvious implementation per module registration path.
- Use `ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull` on public entry points.
- Use complete sentences in XML `<summary>` text; indent with four spaces after the opening tag.

## XML documentation

Required on every type and member under `src/`, including `private` and `internal`. Use `<see cref="..." />`, `<param>`, `<returns>`, `<typeparam>`, and `<value>` as appropriate. Run `dotnet build LiteBus.slnx` and fix SA16xx documentation warnings before finishing.

## Changelog

Update `Changelog.md` under the current major version section when public API or documented behavior changes.
